  "fullContentHtml": "\n<div class=\"ast-post-format- single-layout-1 ast-no-date-box\" style=\"height: auto !important;\">\n<p><!-- .entry-header --></p>\n<div class=\"entry-content clear\" style=\"height: auto !important;\">\n<div class=\"post-desc\">\n<p><span style=\"color: #000000;\"><span style=\"color: #ff0000;\"><strong>Short Information :</strong> <a style=\"color: #ff0000;\" href=\"https://bpsc.bihar.gov.in/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener nofollow\">Bihar Public Service Commission (BPSC)</a> </span>has released the Answer Key for the posts of Assistant Prosecution Officer (APO). This recruitment has been announced for 300 posts. The online application process for BPSC APO Recruitment 2026 were accepted from 27 February 2026, to 20 March 2026. The Examination was conducted on 15 July 2026. Candidates must check the complete details for BPSC APO Answer Key 2026 given below.</span></p>\n</div>\n<div class=\"newtable1\">\n<table style=\"font-size: 16px; font-style: normal; width: 100%;\" width=\"100%\">\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"4\" width=\"100%\">\n<h2 style=\"text-align: center;\"><span style=\"color: #ff0000;\">Bihar Public Service Commission (BPSC)</span></h2>\n<h2 style=\"text-align: center;\"><span style=\"color: #008000;\">BPSC APO Answer Key 2026</span></h2>\n<h2 style=\"text-align: center;\"><span style=\"color: #ff0000;\">Advt.No: 13/2026</span></h2>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td class=\"pd-0\" colspan=\"4\" width=\"100%\">\n<h3 align=\"center\"><span style=\"color: #000000;\"><b>Important Dates</b></span></h3>\n<ul>\n<li><span style=\"color: #000000; font-size: 12pt;\">Application Start Date : <strong>27 February 2026</strong></span></li>\n<li><span style=\"color: #000000; font-size: 12pt;\">Last Date : <strong>20 March 2026</strong></span></li>\n<li><span style=\"color: #000000; font-size: 12pt;\">Fee Payment Last Date : <strong>20 March 2026</strong></span></li>\n<li><span style=\"color: #000000; font-size: 12pt;\">Exam Date : <strong>15 July 2026</strong></span></li>\n<li><span style=\"color: #000000; font-size: 12pt;\">Admit Card : <strong>Available</strong></span></li>\n<li><span style=\"color: #000000; font-size: 12pt;\">Answer Key : <span style=\"color: #ff0000;\"><strong>12 August 2026</strong></span></span></li>\n</ul>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td class=\"pd-0\" colspan=\"4\" width=\"100%\">\n<h3 align=\"center\"><span style=\"color: #000000;\"><b>Application Fee</b></span></h3>\n<ul>\n<li><span style=\"color: #000000; font-size: 12pt;\">All Candidates : <strong>Rs. 100/-</strong></span></li>\n<li><span style=\"font-size: 12pt;\">Bank Charge :&nbsp;<strong>Extra</strong></span></li>\n<li><span style=\"color: #000000; font-size: 12pt;\">Candidates have to pay their Examination Fee Through Debit Card / Credit Card / Net Banking / UPI and Other Fee Payment Mode Only.</span></li>\n</ul>\n<p style=\"text-align: center;\">[adinserter block=”3″]</p>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td class=\"pd-0\" colspan=\"4\" width=\"100%\">\n<h3 style=\"text-align: center;\"><span style=\"color: #000000;\"><strong>BPSC APO Notification 2026 : Age Limit</strong></span></h3>\n<ul>\n<li><span style=\"font-size: 12pt; color: #000000;\"><strong>Age Limit As On 01 August 2026</strong></span></li>\n<li><span style=\"font-size: 12pt; color: #000000;\">Minimum Age :&nbsp;<strong>21 Years</strong></span></li>\n<li><span style=\"font-size: 12pt; color: #000000;\">Maximum Age :&nbsp;<strong>37 Years (UR Male)&nbsp;</strong></span></li>\n<li><span style=\"font-size: 12pt; color: #000000;\">Maximum Age :&nbsp;<strong>40 Years (Female UR, BC, EBC Male &amp; Female)&nbsp;</strong></span></li>\n<li><span style=\"font-size: 12pt; color: #000000;\">Maximum Age :&nbsp;<strong>42 Years (SC, ST Male &amp; Female)</strong></span></li>\n<li><span style=\"color: #000000; font-size: 12pt;\">Age Relaxation as per BPSC APO Recruitment Rules.</span></li>\n<li><span style=\"font-size: 12pt;\">Use <span style=\"color: #000000; background-color: #ffff00;\"> </span>Tool – </span></li>\n</ul>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td class=\"pd-0\" colspan=\"4\" width=\"100%\">\n<h3 style=\"text-align: center;\"><span style=\"color: #000000;\"><strong>BPSC APO 2026 : Vacancy Details</strong></span></h3>\n<p style=\"text-align: center;\"><span style=\"color: #ff0000;\"><strong>Total Posts : 300 Posts</strong></span></p>\n<table style=\"border-collapse: collapse; width: 100%;\">\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td style=\"width: 42.8831%; text-align: center;\"><span style=\"font-size: 12pt; color: #000000;\"><strong>Post Name</strong></span></td>\n<td style=\"width: 29.6498%; text-align: center;\"><span style=\"font-size: 12pt; color: #000000;\"><strong>Category&nbsp;</strong></span></td>\n<td style=\"width: 27.467%; text-align: center;\"><span style=\"font-size: 12pt; color: #000000;\"><strong>No. of Post&nbsp;</strong></span></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td style=\"width: 42.8831%; text-align: center;\" rowspan=\"7\"><span style=\"color: #000000; font-size: 12pt;\">Assistant Prosecution Officer (APO)</span></td>\n<td style=\"width: 29.6498%; text-align: center;\"><span style=\"font-size: 12pt; color: #000000;\">General&nbsp;</span></td>\n<td style=\"width: 27.467%; text-align: center;\"><span style=\"font-size: 12pt; color: #000000;\">129</span></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td style=\"width: 29.6498%; text-align: center;\"><span style=\"font-size: 12pt; color: #000000;\">EWS</span></td>\n<td style=\"width: 27.467%; text-align: center;\"><span style=\"font-size: 12pt; color: #000000;\">29</span></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td style=\"width: 29.6498%; text-align: center;\"><span style=\"font-size: 12pt; color: #000000;\">EBC</span></td>\n<td style=\"width: 27.467%; text-align: center;\"><span style=\"font-size: 12pt; color: #000000;\">64</span></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td style=\"width: 29.6498%; text-align: center;\"><span style=\"font-size: 12pt; color: #000000;\">BC</span></td>\n<td style=\"width: 27.467%; text-align: center;\"><span style=\"font-size: 12pt; color: #000000;\">25</span></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td style=\"width: 29.6498%; text-align: center;\"><span style=\"font-size: 12pt; color: #000000;\">BC-Female</span></td>\n<td style=\"width: 27.467%; text-align: center;\"><span style=\"font-size: 12pt; color: #000000;\">04</span></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td style=\"width: 29.6498%; text-align: center;\"><span style=\"font-size: 12pt; color: #000000;\">SC</span></td>\n<td style=\"width: 27.467%; text-align: center;\"><span style=\"font-size: 12pt; color: #000000;\">42</span></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td style=\"width: 29.6498%; text-align: center;\"><span style=\"font-size: 12pt; color: #000000;\">ST</span></td>\n<td style=\"width: 27.467%; text-align: center;\"><span style=\"font-size: 12pt; color: #000000;\">07</span></td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td class=\"pd-0\" colspan=\"4\" width=\"100%\">\n<h3 align=\"center\"><span style=\"color: #000000;\"><b>BPSC APO Online Form 2026 : Educational Qualification&nbsp;</b></span></h3>\n<ul>\n<li><span style=\"color: #000000; font-size: 12pt;\">Candidates who have Bachelor’s Degree in Law (LLB – 3 Year or 5 Year course) from a recognized University in India.</span></li>\n<li><span style=\"color: #000000; font-size: 12pt;\">All candidates must read the official information completely before applying.</span></li>\n</ul>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td class=\"pd-0\" colspan=\"4\" width=\"100%\">\n<h3 style=\"text-align: center;\"><span style=\"color: #000000;\"><strong>How To Download BPSC APO Answer Key 2026</strong></span></h3>\n<ul>\n<li><span style=\"color: #000000; font-size: 12pt;\">Candidates must go to the&nbsp;<strong>Important Links</strong>&nbsp;section below</span></li>\n<li><span style=\"color: #000000; font-size: 12pt;\">Then the candidates must click on the Answer Key link.&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;&nbsp;</span></li>\n<li><span style=\"color: #000000; font-size: 12pt;\">After clicking on the link, the candidates will be redirected to a new page.</span></li>\n<li><span style=\"color: #000000; font-size: 12pt;\">In this page, candidates have to enter the following details:</span></li>\n<li><span style=\"color: #000000; font-size: 12pt;\">Registration no.</span></li>\n<li><span style=\"color: #000000; font-size: 12pt;\"><strong>Login ID</strong></span></li>\n<li><span style=\"color: #000000; font-size: 12pt;\"><strong>Birth Date/Password</strong></span></li>\n<li><span style=\"color: #000000; font-size: 12pt;\"><strong>Captcha Code</strong></span></li>\n<li><span style=\"color: #000000; font-size: 12pt;\">Then the candidates have to&nbsp; submit the details by clicking on the Login button.</span></li>\n<li><span style=\"color: #000000; font-size: 12pt;\">After successful login, candidates will be able to download the Answer Key.</span></li>\n<li><span style=\"color: #000000; font-size: 12pt;\">Alternatively, the candidates can download the Answer Key from the official website of BPSC also.</span></li>\n</ul>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td class=\"pd-0\" colspan=\"4\" width=\"100%\">\n<h3 style=\"text-align: center;\"><span style=\"color: #000000;\"><strong>BPSC APO Recruitment 2026 : Mode of Selection</strong></span></h3>\n<ul>\n<li><span style=\"font-size: 12pt;\">Pre Exam</span></li>\n<li><span style=\"font-size: 12pt;\">Mains Exam</span></li>\n<li><span style=\"font-size: 12pt;\">Interview</span></li>\n</ul>\n<p style=\"text-align: center;\">[adinserter block=”3″]</p>\n</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n</div>\n<div class=\"newtable2\">\n<table style=\"width: 100%;\">\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td class=\"has-text-align-center\" style=\"text-align: center; padding: 10px 0px;\" colspan=\"4\" data-align=\"center\"><span style=\"color: #cc0052;\"><strong>Follow Our Instagram Channel</strong></span></td>\n<td class=\"post-social-link\" style=\"text-align: center; padding: 10px 0px;\" colspan=\"3\" data-align=\"center\"><strong></strong></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td class=\"has-text-align-center\" style=\"text-align: center;\" colspan=\"4\"